cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BardGPT: A Decoder-Only Shakespeare-Style Language Model Trained From Scratch"
message: "If you use BardGPT in your research, software, or publications, please cite this work."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Singh"
    given-names: "Himanshu"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    email: "himanshusr451tehs@gmail.com"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Himanshu7921/BardGPT"
url: "https://github.com/Himanshu7921/BardGPT"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-01-15"

abstract: >
  BardGPT is a compact, research-grade, decoder-only Transformer trained 
  from scratch on the Tiny Shakespeare corpus. It provides a transparent, 
  extensible architecture for studying GPT-style models, including causal 
  self-attention, sinusoidal positional embeddings, AdamW optimization, 
  warmup+cosine scheduling, and full checkpoint reproducibility.

keywords:
  - GPT
  - Transformer
  - Decoder-only model
  - Shakespeare
  - Character-level modeling
  - Language modeling
  - Deep learning
  - PyTorch

